nfig state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id 74bdea6a with pdns_recursor listening and DNS config present captured pre-restart (cmd-251726094f4d49b0). Reboot scheduled and acknowledged (cmd-28d653910d154f00); new boot_id 1cab613a confirmed post-restart (cmd-68041cf400e74e88); DNS service/config verified intact after restart (cmd-8d88b418316e4034). Cross-checked against fixed after_executor snapshot showing boot-identity change and pdns_recursor listening.","evidence_ids":["cmd-251726094f4d49b0","cmd-28d653910d154f00","cmd-68041cf400e74e88","cmd-8d88b418316e4034","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"req-7","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: node2 healthy baseline -> restart -> changed boot identity -> recovered DNS resolution state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id dfeb3b70 with successful inventory.internal resolution captured pre-restart (cmd-3d585f9777574fde). Reboot acknowledged (cmd-6015d26cbfb14814); new boot_id b5055f9e confirmed post-restart (cmd-9528785548c3410c); resolvectl confirmed DNS server 10.100.42.10 plus successful resolution post-restart (cmd-0ff6ce42521c4590). Cross-checked against fixed after_executor snapshot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3d585f9777574fde","cmd-6015d26cbfb14814","cmd-9528785548c3410c","cmd-0ff6ce42521c4590","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"req-8","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: node3 healthy baseline -> restart -> changed boot identity -> recovered DNS resolution state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id bdd5de93 captured pre-restart (cmd-2df284b0433f4ed4). Reboot acknowledged (cmd-bd889ceb52974f12); new boot_id 11a6b264 confirmed post-restart (cmd-e5eb65316c944496); resolvectl confirmed DNS server 10.100.42.10 plus successful resolution post-restart (cmd-ce300e11847748ef). Cross-checked against fixed after_executor snapshot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2df284b0433f4ed4","cmd-bd889ceb52974f12","cmd-e5eb65316c944496","cmd-ce300e11847748ef","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity"]},{"id":"req-9","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: node4 healthy baseline -> restart -> changed boot identity -> recovered control-node/tooling state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id 7051d0bc with ansible tooling and playbook files present captured pre-restart (cmd-78a792aba462426e). Reboot acknowledged (cmd-cb9b2d53e0c04c72); new boot_id 8c927326 confirmed post-restart (cmd-f5fc9c6a70d847fa); a full idempotent ansible-playbook re-run succeeded with changed=0 post-restart, proving tooling and cluster DNS state survived (cmd-13049160ea304736).","evidence_ids":["cmd-78a792aba462426e","cmd-cb9b2d53e0c04c72","cmd-f5fc9c6a70d847fa","cmd-13049160ea304736","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.92,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"Most state-changing commands trace clearly to task prerequisites (SSH key setup, sshd host-key regeneration to fix a broken sshd on node2/node3), the DNS configuration itself, or bounded verification/restart evidence. Some unnecessary mutations occurred: node1's DNS forwarding config was deleted and recommitted twice (cmd-1ef5016c017447f8, cmd-8f9ef15c95d94afa) as troubleshooting steps while diagnosing a sudo/become permission issue, each followed by a manual re-apply (cmd-e71b5dc64fac48d3, cmd-6ff2bb12c37e45f6) outside the Ansible playbook before the final idempotent Ansible run (cmd-0ffce1d6ff9b4619) established the definitive state. These cycles were bounded, low-risk, and left no residue, but represent avoidable extra apply/delete/reapply churn from an initially misconfigured inventory (ansible_become=no for a sudo-capable VyOS user). Final state matches the intended configuration and the after_executor snapshot shows no failed services and consistent package health across all nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a21d7fab79e744c6","cmd-1ef5016c017447f8","cmd-8f9ef15c95d94afa","cmd-e5216cfda0d845a2","cmd-e71b5dc64fac48d3","cmd-6ff2bb12c37e45f6","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor successfully implemented node1 as a VyOS-based DNS resolver via Ansible from the control node (node4): it answers inventory.internal with node2's address (10.100.42.11) through a static-host-mapping and forwards all other queries to the upstream gateway (10.100.42.1) via 'service dns forwarding'. node2 and node3 were reconfigured via Ansible (systemd-networkd DNS=/Domains=~./UseDNS=no) to resolve exclusively through node1, and end-to-end resolution of both inventory.internal and public domains (example.com) was directly verified on both clients. All four managed nodes underwent the restart evidence protocol with clear baseline boot-identity, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot-identity, and recovered DNS/tooling state, cross-checked against the fixed after_executor lifecycle snapshot. All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct, first-party evidence rather than executor claims alone.","limitations":["Command outputs are bounded/truncated in places (e.g., cmd-a5241d2c43194960 truncated 12321 characters), so some intermediate diagnostic detail could not be fully reviewed, though this did not affect assessment of material outcomes.","The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare since prepare was disabled, so preparer-vs-executor separation relies entirely on the executor's own before/after actions rather than an independent prepare-phase baseline.","Two mid-task troubleshooting cycles on node1 (delete+reapply of DNS forwarding config) were observed due to an initial ansible_become misconfiguration; fully corrected with no residue, but add churn to the audit trail before the final idempotent playbook run succeeded."]},"ttft_ms":3232,"type":"result","duration_ms":83744,"uuid":"b7cae57d-7bf1-4ba3-b62c-a0fdccfa8b93","ttft_stream_ms":2759,"time_to_request_ms":199,"first_content_frame_ms":2759,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
